LocalAI llama.cpp grpc-server: keep independent IMAGE media parts independent.

The pinned mtmd splitter omits empty text between adjacent media markers and the pinned
merge rule temporally merges two adjacent non-audio bitmaps of equal dimensions, so a
reconstructed message carrying independent IMAGE parts pairs adjacent equal-sized
stills. Insert a neutral ordinal non-whitespace text boundary between independent
media parts, and between the final independent IMAGE and a following VIDEO when no audio
intervenes. The user prompt bytes, the single-media layout, audio routing, and the
deliberate lazy frame expansion inside one video are unchanged.

Authored working-tree patch applied to the prepared tree that is actually compiled; the
pinned LocalAI and llama.cpp source commits are unchanged. Apply it with
scripts/localai-llamacpp-independent-images-patch.mjs, which fails closed on any other
header shape and is safe to re-run.

